at first glance this looks like a  completely normal beach resort it's 7  a.m. and the loungers are neatly packed  away the clothes hooks ready for a new  day of bathing time to give Trieste  speech pool a quick tidy up before the  guests arrive the regular guests are  already waiting to get in like what  melaa veero samosa is best in the  morning we always have the same lounges  the pool opens at 7:30 just like many  others in the area but there was one  major difference women and children  enter to the left the men to the right  maura bc aki makes sure everyone abides  by the rules when she's not controlling  the tickets she takes care of the cash  desk the pool attendant knows many of  her customers habits many women just  come for a couple of hours at midday to  sunbathe and relax separated from the  men on the other side this wall keeps  men and women apart and the women's side  is often much busier than the men's a  ticket for the pool still costs a modest  1 euro if the City Council decided to  privatize the pool because it's not  profitable there would be a revolution  in Trieste and Miko would be among those  in the uprising she's one of the younger  regular visitors but is just as much in  favour of upholding traditions as the  older guests  the women are glad the wall is there to  separate them from the men it protects  them from curious glances if you have a  bit of spare tire after the winter and  aren't in the best shape you have stress  and less problems then he would have on  a normal beach where men can look at you  you feel a lot freer a hundred and ten  years ago the female bathers were still  completely covered up Trieste was under  Austrian rule back then the so-called  Lantana pool below the lighthouse opened  in 1903 complete with the dividing wall  it survived two world wars Austrians  Italians Germans and Yugoslavians and  has also outlived some unsavory episodes  in history after World War one my  grandfather got rid of his lice hair  before he came back home in wartime the  soldiers washed on one side and washed  their horses on the other  fortunately times have changed but men  are still men Mattie Claudio is trying  to persuade the ladies to meet up in the  water through a slit in the wall they  might be separated on the beach but the  men and women can mingle freely in the  water  if your wife asks you who the blonde was  you were talking to in the water that  can lead to arguments like most of the  people here the 74 year old has been  coming since he was a child but things  aren't always this peaceful people often  fight for the best spot on the beach I  try to persuade the regulars that they  don't have a right to reserved spots  that's the rule here but peace normally  returns by the end of the day now the  pool is left to the seagulls and the  Bano Lanterna is ready for another day
 

